rl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1016365?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS","html_url":"https://github.com/PatrickJS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-08-03T11:15:49Z","updated_at":"2018-01-14T05:17:13Z","body":"The idea for the alternative syntax is legacy html and user familiarity. For example, we're able to create components/directives that work both in angular 1 and angular 2 following the same interface. This is due to the fact that angular 1 didn't enforce any conventions (since no one knew what the best practices were for component/directives 6 years ago). So we can actually take advantage of this today\r\n(I gave a subtle nod to a migration technique during [ng-vegas](https://youtu.be/x296y5mErWI?t=9m36s))\r\n\r\nng1 https://github.com/gdi2290/ng-vegas-angular2-d3/blob/master/angular1/app.js#L10\r\nng2 https://github.com/gdi2290/ng-vegas-angular2-d3/blob/master/app.ts#L60\r\n\r\nessentially we can create a directive that works in both ng1 and ng2 with this example\r\n\r\n``` html\r\n<bar-graph\r\n  bind-data=\"graphData\"\r\n  width=\"500\"\r\n  height=\"130\">\r\n</bar-graph>\r\n```\r\n\r\nNotice how we're using the alternative syntax but we can do this for angular 1 today using the alias\r\n`scope: { data: '=bindData' }`. We create a directive for each event already in angular 1 (legacy) so it does make sense to continue down that path. Doing this allows you to delete half your code (ng2 means twice as good since it's half the code?) when switching to angular 2 (now that we know what the best practices are)\r\n\r\n[![github-tipe-logo](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1016365/34912701-7edec34c-f89c-11e7-8c89-bed6cef064b5.png)](https://tipe.io?ref=github-comment)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/127197865/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"PatrickJS","id":1016365,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTYzNjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1016365?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS","html_url":"https://github.com/PatrickJS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PatrickJS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":375627817,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDM3NTYyNzgxNw==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/events/375627817","actor":{"login":"mhevery","id":111951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTk1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"ht